Facility Placement Planner is the deterministic facility placement planning and
explanation authority for DCCP Tranche 2 (Facility Capacity and Placement). It is
built from the C++20 standard library only.

Third-party components
----------------------

None. No third-party source code, library, header, or generated artefact is
included in, linked into, or required by this product.

The build depends only on the platform's own toolchain and operating system:

  * the C++20 standard library of the toolchain that builds the project;
  * the operating system's file, locking, and process primitives, used for the
    durable store and reached through the platform API (CreateFileW, LockFileEx,
    MoveFileExW, and FlushFileBuffers on Windows; open, flock, fsync, and rename
    elsewhere).

No network service, telemetry endpoint, analytics library, or runtime package
manager is contacted or required at build time or at run time.

What this product is not
------------------------

It is not a physical hardware controller and does not claim any hardware proof. It
does not contain, generate, or depend on PDU, UPS, generator, cooling-equipment,
GPU, multi-node, or RDMA evidence of any kind. Its benchmarks are labelled
SYNTHETIC because they are generated from a fixed seed on the machine that ran
them. Where a claim rests on an operating-system facility rather than on hardware,
it is stated as such.

